# Gradle
.gradle/
build/

# Kotlin/JS yarn lockfile dir (checks/*). Deliberately NOT committed: a
# bare `yarn.lock` (no package.json) makes GitHub's dependency graph raise
# npm Dependabot alerts on dev-toolchain transitives that are NEVER shipped
# (the plugin ships only java-diff-utils at runtime; BCV is compileOnly),
# plus daily-aborting security-update runs. The `.d.ts` baselines are
# Kotlin-compiler-derived, so npm-toolchain pinning protects nothing the
# checks assert. Kotlin regenerates the store per build. Escape hatch if a
# floating npm transitive ever breaks a check build: rename the lock via
# `YarnRootExtension.lockFileName` (unindexed name) and re-commit it.
kotlin-js-store/

# JVM/Android
local.properties
# Heap dumps from `-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError` (set in the Gradle
# daemon JVM opts) land in the daemon's CWD — typically a check-cell
# project root, NOT under `build/`. Ignore globally.
*.hprof

